└── synchronous HTTP client for polling REST gateway
    ├── Candidates : requests, httpx
    ├── Used APIs  : Session, session.get, resp.raise_for_status, resp.json
    ├── Pitfalls   : httpx.Client() vs requests.Session() have different construction/config options (e.g. base_url handling, timeout defaults); Exception 
    │   types differ: requests.exceptions.HTTPError vs httpx.HTTPStatusError; httpx supports both sync and async clients; must ensure sync Client is used to 
    │   preserve behavior, not AsyncClient; Timeout semantics differ: httpx timeout is more granular (connect/read/write/pool) vs requests single float timeout
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── requests.Session is used to issue GET requests with a timeout, check status, and parse JSON. httpx offers a Client/Session-like object with a very 
        similar sync API (client.get, raise_for_status, .json()) and can serve as a drop-in replacement for this synchronous usage pattern, though not without 
        code changes.

